s/09/0927f7a957a2a5d8b91aafd71e488ce535f2c8ada2ef97d0592d58b75cd2eece.png)\n\nFrom the diagram above, which of the following statements is true?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447464 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1f0a9542-3ba4-5c20-945c-8b2a173ef94b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447464 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are two lines. Then,\n\n- $a∥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are parallel, and\n\n- $a⊥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are perpendicular.\n\nIn the given diagram, there are two pairs of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $s$ is perpendicular to $t,$ which we write as $s⊥t$\n\n- $w$ is perpendicular to $t,$ which we write as $w⊥t.$\n\n![](images/75/756f579f20695c46394e6667fd78444504b1470619ea6ca4b68eed87eeed934e.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct statement is $s⊥t$ and $w⊥t.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447466 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447466 #edb/ref 1069 "q-153412" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447466 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447466 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e8/e8caa8e283c60d845c4b8fbe2c352818d300b51748f37b9788eac0bf1e73b7d5.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447466 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2d6731a9-4b1d-5a58-8690-9d08ea615462" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447466 #edb/ref 1074 "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that we have two sets of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{PU}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{PQ}$\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{RS}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{ST}$\n\n![](images/24/2492594432bf29b2753d646c53b66ffd6230c21db71c4dd12479c9811217dc91.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{UP}$ and $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are perpendicular, and $\\overset{―}{RS}$ and $\\overset{―}{ST}$ are also perpendicular. We can write this as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $\\overset{―}{UP}⊥\\overset{―}{PQ}$ and $\\overset{―}{RS}⊥\\overset{―}{ST}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447467 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447467 #edb/ref 1069 "q-151183" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447467 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447467 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fa/fa8cae4093f218e9df7859a1eb0ebf036b1d07fd7963042b8d66557f6842ccd6.png)\n\nList all of the parallel lines in the diagram above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447467 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b9ce7e4-46a6-59bd-8550-ab45a107e732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447467 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/40/4095a3e6206ed53b49eb411ef3b7a279bfa68e68bdd0abafa624161f78bc11cb.png)\n\nTwo lines are parallel if they never intersect.\n\nIn the given diagram, the only parallel lines are $l$ and $m.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447468 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447468 #edb/ref 1069 "q-153263" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447468 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447468 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/de/de307da2bc912e9eb6f7312a16be40908d6ccd43cbc613367d042ed55090f2ee.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, which of the following statements is true?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447468 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "838db218-c7b5-5ab1-b5e1-0abd38558574" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447468 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose $p$ and $q$ are two lines. Then,\n\n- $p∥q$ means $p$ and $q$ are parallel, and\n\n- $p⊥q$ means $p$ and $q$ are perpendicular.\n\nThe lines $a,c$ and $b,d$ are parallel since they will never intersect. Therefore, the correct statement is $a∥c$ and $b∥d.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447469 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447469 #edb/ref 1069 "q-151168" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447469 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447469 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/94/940a6996800ee85745643b34e429bb1fa85064bbab94f52bed328b074024fd22.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447469 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86e173f6-09d0-539e-96a4-71b8b3120bde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447469 #edb/ref 1074 "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that the lines $\\overset{⟷}{EA}$ and  $\\overset{⟷}{AB}$ are perpendicular.\n\n![](images/81/81e84f9f6f3f50f6a5ef3f39381ebce028ccb52fa09b2d7042c9206a7027f337.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{EA}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ are perpendicular. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{EA}⊥\\overset{―}{AB}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447471 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447471 #edb/ref 1069 "q-151162" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447471 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447471 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/49/495da285b0971f050ad2baa2031ef27a9d9fd719078f535559cb2795057516de.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447471 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b26db26d-7241-5602-a20a-a5953a1b2569" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447471 #edb/ref 1074 "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that the lines $\\overset{⟷}{PQ}$ and  $\\overset{⟷}{TP}$ are perpendicular.\n\n![](images/db/db4497b62f456afacd78221d68a76200d18dedcfd1e3e7b73f64847e39a55ae9.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{TP}$ and $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are perpendicular. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{TP}⊥\\overset{―}{PQ}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447474 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447474 #edb/ref 1069 "q-151165" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447474 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447474 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d8/d8af8bd4c928216d30d6ee1764139a86af1f7ac2ce6a01d9b98cb081a60ed322.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447474 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e371cbf5-7ac9-5e8f-8f0f-f99fbc339fe5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447474 #edb/ref 1074 "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that we have two sets of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{AB}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{BC}$\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{EA}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{AB}$\n\n![](images/90/90902346a26d5120e13c3df8e841e4fb57c6006b6e6a4390e30c6ae41f18630c.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are perpendicular, and $\\overset{―}{EA}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ are also perpendicular. We can write this as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $\\overset{―}{AB}⊥\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{EA}⊥\\overset{―}{AB}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447475 #edb/ref 1069 "q-153499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447475 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447475 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/86/8666a8c28b50deb88fc9e7cca3951b9d5fab9d8d07ede6abac774f41271324b5.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the parallel sides." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447475 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f045e30a-5c77-5aee-853f-bedc4016f900" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447475 #edb/ref 1074 "Two lines are parallel if they never intersect.\n\nNow, let's examine the direction of the sides in the figure to determine whether any pair lies along parallel lines.\n\nNotice that the sides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{DE}$ both lie along horizontal lines. The remaining sides have different directions, so they do not form any additional pair of parallel sides.\n\n![](images/7f/7f55b88378fe0e9389ea7a540cc40a02c9e619854a6815e9700b808770fa3a13.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{DE}$ are parallel. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{DE}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
